TASK-210 runtime harness: Quick Detour's page settings popover, the bar's
drag-or-click buttons, the Open in dropdown without its subtitle, and the
palette prompt; the main window's site settings after the shared builder.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR;
DETOUR_VERIFY_APPEARANCE light or dark; DETOUR_VERIFY_FIXTURE a loopback
server (python3 -I -m http.server 8936 over a dir with index.html, title
"Lookup Page"); DETOUR_VERIFY_EXT an unpacked MV3 extension with an action
popup ("Verify Probe"), installed with ExtensionManager.install(from:) and
pinned in Default. Data dir DetourVerify2100.

Real input: NSApp.postEvent clicks and keys, and real HID presses
(CGEvent .cghidEventTap: move, down, 12 dragged steps, up, then the cursor
warped back) for the drags and the plain click; the Accessibility grant made
HID drags work on 2026-10-26. Every activation and posted input waits for
12 s of HID idle. Captures are of Detour's own windows (-l) or regions over
them (-R). run.sh tails the log for "SHOOT <name> <window>" / "SHOOTRECT
<name> x,y,w,h" (zsh: split with ${=line#*SHOOT }) and kills only the PID it
launched after "done".

    git apply docs/harness/task210-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    run.sh light; run.sh dark
    git apply -R docs/harness/task210-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Results (2026-10-26, light and dark, screen unlocked): the bar shows the
pinned probe, the Site Settings button (slider) and Copy Link; a click opens
the main window's popover below it (host 127.0.0.1, no resources blocked,
the three switches, "Verify Probe [pinned]", Extension Settings…). Its
blocking switch whitelisted 127.0.0.1 in Default only (not Second) and the
page reloaded (a JS marker gone); again: un-whitelisted, reloaded. The
probe's name closed the settings and opened its popup below the pinned
button (it opened above, out of the window, before the edge fix). A click
on the host opened the palette, "Search or enter a URL" when emptied; the
main window's Cmd+T palette "Where do you want to go?". The Open in
dropdown: Default: Home ⌘O / Second: Play, no subtitles. A posted press
moving 12 pt on the host began the window drag (no palette); HID drags of
80/40 pt on the host and on Open in moved the window (no palette, the page
not moved); a HID click on the host opened the palette. With the main
window key, a first HID click on the Quick Detour's Open in only made it
key (page kept, Home's tab count unchanged); a first HID drag moved it. The
main window's popover (shared builder): same content, its blocking toggle
reloaded the main tab and was undone.
Not checked: a page with blocked resources (count > 0), several displays,
VoiceOver, a person's own hand.

